  <section id="dining">
    <h2>Dining</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>1900 Park Fare</strong> is the character buffet, branded as Wish Makers Enchanted Dining. Breakfast is listed at 8:00 a.m. to 12:00 p.m., and dinner at 4:00 p.m. to 9:00 p.m. Disney says characters may include Cinderella, Tiana, Aladdin and Mirabel, and that appearances can change. <span class="verify">[verify hours still current]</span></li>
      <li><strong>Grand Floridian Cafe</strong> is table service for breakfast, lunch and dinner. It reopened in November 2026 after a mid-year refurbishment. Dinner was listed at 5:00 p.m. to 9:00 p.m. when we checked. <span class="verify">[verify hours still current]</span></li>
      <li><strong>Cítricos</strong> and <strong>Narcoossee's</strong> are table-service restaurants. Narcoossee's sits on the water, by the boat dock. <strong>Victoria &amp; Albert's</strong> is the fine-dining restaurant; book well ahead if that is part of your trip.</li>
      <li><strong>Gasparilla Island Grill</strong> is the quick-service restaurant.</li>
      <li><strong>Enchanted Rose</strong> and <strong>Garden View Lounge</strong> are the lounges. Garden View is known for afternoon tea.</li>
      <li>You can use mobile ordering in the My Disney Experience app at the quick-service spots.</li>
      <li><strong>Park dining reservations:</strong> Disney resort guests can book their whole stay (up to 10 nights) starting 60 days before arrival. 1900 Park Fare and Victoria &amp; Albert's book up, so plan ahead.</li>
    </ul>
    <span class="ryan">[Ryan: your go-to meal here, and one thing you'd skip.]</span>
  </section>

  <section id="pools">
    <h2>Pools and things to do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Beach Pool</strong> is the main pool. Disney lists it at 111,261 gallons, overlooking the Seven Seas Lagoon, with a 181-foot slide, cascading waterfalls, zero-depth entry, a walking bridge, a lounge and bar, and a splash area for little kids. Cabanas can be rented. This is the busy one.</li>
      <li><strong>Courtyard Pool</strong> is a quieter, heated zero-entry leisure pool behind the main building. It goes down to nearly 5 feet and has a whirlpool spa next to it.</li>
      <li>Towels are free at the pools. Life jackets are available at The Captain's Shipyard. Hours and lifeguard coverage vary and can change.</li>
      <li>There is also a spa on site.</li>
    </ul>
