  <section id="booking">
    <h2>Booking and value tips</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Start with a Resort View room if the view is not the point.</strong> In 2026 those rooms ran from $832 to $1,370 a night at full price including tax, depending on dates. That is the lowest hotel rate at this resort.</li>
      <li><strong>Pay more for Water View or Theme Park View only if you will use it.</strong> Water View rooms ran about $864 to $1,506. Theme Park View was higher still. Confirm you are in an outer building if that is what you booked, and think about the walk.</li>
      <li><strong>Club Level is a different product.</strong> You are paying for the lounge, and some Club rooms are larger. Compare that cost with eating some of those meals at Grand Floridian Cafe or Gasparilla.</li>
      <li><strong>Extra adults cost more.</strong> Deluxe rates assume two adults. Each extra adult adds $35 a night plus tax, and kids under 18 are free.</li>
      <li><strong>Check Disney's own offers page first.</strong> Disney points to <a href="https://disneyworld.disney.go.com/special-offers/">its special offers page</a> for discounts. Our deals hub will track current ones.</li>
      <li><strong>Lightning Lane head start:</strong> Disney resort guests can buy Lightning Lane passes up to 7 days before their stay.</li>
    </ul>
